# Every wall-clock bound a test asserts, with its numbers: tools/check/wall-bounds.py says what a site is and what each
# verdict means. <path> | <function> | <bound> | <count> | <verdict> | good <d>, bad <d> | <reason>. good: how long the
# path the test expects takes on an idle machine; bad: how long the path the bound is to catch takes.
kuicksilver-engine-interop/src/jvmTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/engineinterop/WebSocketPairSuite.kt | closingEndsWithTheServerClosingFirst | <3s | 1 | separated | good 0.3s, bad 5s | good: open the session and close it, the server closing TCP first and the client following at once, about 0.3 s per order; bad: a client left waiting out its close wait for the server's FIN (ours: T2, WEBSOCKET_CLOSE_WAIT_MILLIS 5 s)
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/appleTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/pac/PacEngineAppleTest.kt | negative_endlessScriptStopsAtTheCap | <4s | 1 | separated | good 0.1s, bad 5s | good: the download stops at PAC_MAX_SCRIPT_BYTES (1 MiB) of a loopback body, well under 0.1 s; bad: a download that reads the endless body runs until the lookup's 5 000 ms timeout passed to PacScripts.script
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/appleTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/pac/PacEngineAppleTest.kt | negative_pacUrlThatHangsTimesOut | <1s | 1 | justified | good 0s, bad 5s | good: the second lookup answers from the remembered failure in the cache, no network and no timer, a few microseconds; bad: a forgotten failure makes the lookup wait the hanging server out to its 5 000 ms timeout; the bound is under 2 s so not separated, but a cache read cannot take 1 s on a loaded machine
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/ClientDnsTest.kt | negative_aCancellationTheDnsThrowsFailsTheCall | <30s | 1 | separated | good 0.1s, bad 60s | good: the resolver's own CancellationException fails the request and the WebSocket at once, about 0.02 s observed for the whole test; bad: the WebSocket waits for an answer that never comes until the engine's connectTimeout of 60 s
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/ClientDnsTest.kt | negative_anUnusableLiteralIsNeverConnected | <20s | 1 | separated | good 0.1s, bad 30s | good: the 0.0.0.0 literal is refused before any packet, about 0.02 s observed for the whole test; bad: an attempt to the unusable address that only ends at the engine's connectTimeout of 30 s
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/ClientDnsTest.kt | negative_aStalledDnsEndsAtTheConnectTimeout | <10s | 1 | separated | good 0.3s, bad 60s | good: the stalled lookup is cancelled at the configured connectTimeout of 300 ms (about 0.6 s observed for both modes); bad: a lookup outside the connect timeout never ends, so the call hangs until clientTest's 60 s withTimeout
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/ClientDnsTest.kt | negative_aSystemAnswerOfTheUnspecifiedAddressIsNeverConnected | <20s | 1 | separated | good 0.5s, bad 30s | good: the 0.0.0.0 answer is refused before any packet, about 0.4 s observed for the whole test with both modes; bad: an attempt to the unusable address that only ends at the engine's connectTimeout of 30 s
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/ClientFallbackTest.kt | blockedUdpFallsBackAfterHardDelayAndMarksBroken | <2s | 1 | separated | good 0.6s, bad 10s | good: HTTP/1.1 starts after the 250 ms default head start (ProtocolRace.headStart, no RTT known) and at the latest when QUIC fails at its 500 ms handshakeTimeout, then reuses the pooled connection; bad: no fallback until the engine's default connectTimeout of 10 s
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/ClientH1Test.kt | connectTimeoutMapsToKtor | <10s | 1 | justified | good 0.3s, bad 60s | upper side of a two-sided window: good is the request's HttpTimeout connectTimeoutMillis of 300 ms, bad is the engine's connectTimeout of 60 s; the 10 s side is 9.7 s above the good path, so a loaded machine cannot reach it
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/ClientH1Test.kt | connectTimeoutMapsToKtor | >=250ms | 1 | justified | good 0.3s, bad 0s | lower side of a two-sided window: good is the request's 300 ms HttpTimeout, bad is a failure before the connect step ran, near 0 s; the 300 ms timer starts inside c.get after the mark, so the elapsed time is at least 300 ms however loaded the machine
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/ClientH2WebSocketTest.kt | negative_theTransportWaitCountsFromBothCloses | <5s | 1 | justified | good 3s, bad 6s | upper side of a window: END_STREAM one 3 s close wait after the server's Close, against two close waits; 2 s of headroom over the good path and 1 s under the bad one
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/ClientH2WebSocketTest.kt | negative_theTransportWaitCountsFromBothCloses | >2s | 1 | justified | good 3s, bad 1s | lower side of a window: END_STREAM one 3 s close wait after the server's Close, against 1 s left of a deadline counted from the client's own Close; a loaded machine only makes the good path longer
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/ClientH2WebSocketTest.kt | negative_theTransportWaitCountsFromBothCloses | >1.5s | 1 | separated | good 3s, bad 0s | good: the reset with CANCEL one 3 s close wait after END_STREAM; bad: the reset right after END_STREAM
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/ClientHappyEyeballsTest.kt | h3RacesTheAddressesOfAName | <10s | 1 | separated | good 0.4s, bad 20s | good: the silent ::1 attempt and, one connection attempt delay later, the winning 127.0.0.1 QUIC handshake, about 0.35 s observed; bad: HTTP/3 tries the first address only and H3Only fails at the configured connectTimeout of 20 s
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/ClientHappyEyeballsTest.kt | negative_aStalledAaaaQueryDoesNotHoldTheConnection | <10s | 1 | separated | good 0.1s, bad 20s | good: the A answer waits at most the Resolution Delay (RFC 8305, 50 ms) for the stalled AAAA, then connects over IPv4, about 0.06 s observed; bad: the connection waits for the AAAA query until the configured connectTimeout of 20 s
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/ClientHappyEyeballsTest.kt | negative_aWebSocketOverH3TakesTheConnectionsAddressWithoutALookup | <10s | 1 | separated | good 0.1s, bad 20s | good: the WebSocket keys its CONNECTING lock by the live connection's address with no lookup, about 0.11 s observed; bad: a fresh lookup of the name stalls and the WebSocket waits until the configured connectTimeout of 20 s
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/ClientHappyEyeballsTest.kt | webSocketWithAStalledAaaa | <10s | 1 | separated | good 0.2s, bad 20s | good: the WebSocket keys its lock by the families that answered and connects over IPv4, about 0.13 s (H1) and 0.17 s (H3) observed; bad: the keys wait for the stalled AAAA until the configured connectTimeout of 20 s (over H3 for good, ended by clientTest's 60 s)
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/ClientOrderlyCloseTest.kt | negative_socketTimeoutFiresOnTimeAgainstAHungServer | <10s | 1 | separated | good 0.3s, bad 30.3s | good: the 300 ms socket timeout after the server read the request; bad: the orderly close in front of the exception, its bound stretched to 30 s here
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/ClientWebSocketConnectingTest.kt | negative_stalledHandshakeTimesOutAndFreesTheAddress | <5s | 1 | separated | good 0.5s, bad 60s | good: the opening handshake that never gets its 101 fails at the configured connectTimeout of 500 ms; bad: nothing bounds the wait for the 101, so the call hangs until clientTest's 60 s withTimeout
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/ClientWebTransportTest.kt | negative_sessionsWaitingForAFailedSetupFailWithinOneTimeout | <6s | 1 | separated | good 4s, bad 8s | good: all six sessions fail within one 4 s connect timeout; bad: two timeouts in series or more
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/contract/DownloadTest.kt | testDownloadWithSlowConsumer | <10s | 1 | separated | good 1s, bad 120s | good: a 4 MiB loopback download minus the consumer's measured delays, under 1 s per the test's comment (1.3-1.4 s observed for the whole test over all modes); bad: a transfer stalled on flow control or the engine, ended only by the harness timeout of 2 minutes
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/dns/DnsMessageTest.kt | negative_hostileLargestAnswerIsReadInLinearTime | <5s | 1 | separated | good 10ms, bad 20s | good: one linear read of the 65 535-byte message, about 10 ms observed; bad: walking every name for every new TargetName, tens of seconds at this size per the test's comment
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/dns/SvcbRecordTest.kt | tenThousandMandatoryKeysParse | <2s | 1 | justified | good 10ms, bad 1s | smoke check: good is two parses of the 10 000-key record, about 6 ms observed, nearly 2 s under the bound so load cannot fail it; bad is the quadratic mandatory check (about 5 x 10^7 key reads, estimated well under 1 s on the JVM), which negative_mandatoryCheckReadsEachKeyAtMostOnce catches by its read count, not by time
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/jvmTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/ClientEarlyDataTest.kt | earlyConnectionDoesNotWinTheRaceOnAnUnconfirmedNetwork | <10s | 1 | separated | good 0.1s, bad 20s | good: on the unconfirmed network HTTP/1.1 wins at once, about 0.04 s observed for the whole test; bad: the 0-RTT connection wins the race over blocked UDP and the request falls back only at the configured connectTimeout of 20 s
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/jvmTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/ClientEarlyDataTest.kt | postWaitingForAFailedHandshakeFallsBack | <15s | 1 | separated | good 3s, bad 30s | good: the POST waiting for the handshake falls back at the configured connectTimeout of 3 s (3.03-3.08 s observed for the whole test); bad: it waits for the QUIC handshakeTimeout of 30 s
kuicksilver-ktor-client/src/jvmTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/client/ClientEarlyDataTest.kt | udpBlockedWith0RttFallsBackWithinConnectTimeout | <15s | 1 | separated | good 3s, bad 30s | good: the 0-RTT GET over blocked UDP falls back at the configured connectTimeout of 3 s (3.03-3.06 s observed for the whole test); bad: it waits for the QUIC handshakeTimeout of 30 s
kuicksilver-ktor-server/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/server/ServerH2Test.kt | gracefulStopTwoPhaseGoAway | <10s | 1 | separated | good 0.1s, bad 30s | good: the stop returns once the client's close_notify ended the TLS close; bad: a server that ignores it waits its close bound, stretched to 30 s here
kuicksilver-ktor-server/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/server/ServerH3Test.kt | stopSendsGoAwayToAllConnectionsAtOnce | <2.5s | 1 | separated | good 0.4s, bad 5s | good: one round of the server's 50 ms wait between its two GOAWAYs for all 100 connections, about 0.2 s and up to 0.4 s seen; bad: one round per connection, 100 rounds of 50 ms
kuicksilver-ktor-server/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/server/ServerH3Test.kt | stopWaitsForInFlightH3Call | <10s | 1 | separated | good 0.1s, bad 30s | good: the stop returns once the released call finished; bad: a stop that waits out its 30 s grace period
kuicksilver-ktor-server/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/server/ServerObservabilityTest.kt | aConnectionAcceptedDuringStopGetsGoAwayAndTheStopEndsEarly | <10s | 1 | separated | good 0.1s, bad 20s | good: the late connection gets GOAWAY and the stop ends once it is idle, about 0.1 s observed; bad: the stop waits out the whole 20 000 ms grace period (the test's withTimeout of 10 s ends it first)
kuicksilver-ktor-server/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/server/ServerObservabilityTest.kt | stopAtTheGraceDeadlineClosesWithH3NoError | <3s | 1 | separated | good 0.3s, bad 60s | good: stop(300, 3000) closes what is left at the 300 ms grace deadline, about 0.32 s observed for the whole test; bad: a stop that waits for the in-flight call, whose handler sleeps 60 s
kuicksilver-ktor-server/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/server/ServerObservabilityTest.kt | stopRefusesNewHttp3ClientsWhileInFlightCallsFinish | <10s | 1 | separated | good 0.5s, bad 30s | good: the late client refused at its first Initial with CONNECTION_REFUSED, under a second; bad: a client never refused, which gives up at its 30 s handshake timeout
kuicksilver-ktor-server/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/server/ServerWebSocketCloseOrderTest.kt | h3Close | >4s | 1 | separated | good 5s, bad 0s | good: STOP_SENDING H3_NO_ERROR comes when the server's close wait ends, WebSocketOverH2.CLOSE_WAIT 5 s after its FIN (5.1 s observed for the whole test); bad: STOP_SENDING right after the server's own FIN, near 0 s
kuicksilver-ktor-server/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/server/ServerWebSocketCloseOrderTest.kt | negative_h3BytesAfterTheClientsCloseAreDroppedNotBuffered | >4s | 1 | separated | good 5s, bad 0s | good: the post-Close bytes are dropped and STOP_SENDING H3_NO_ERROR comes when WebSocketOverH2.CLOSE_WAIT (5 s) ends, 5.0-5.1 s observed for the whole test; bad: the stream stopped right after the server's FIN, near 0 s
kuicksilver-ktor-server/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/server/ServerWebSocketCloseOrderTest.kt | tlsFinComesAtOnce | <10s | 1 | separated | good 0.1s, bad 30s | good: the server's FIN right after its close_notify; bad: a FIN held for the client's close_notify, which waits the accepted socket's close bound, stretched to 30 s here
kuicksilver-ktor-server/src/jvmTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/ktor/server/StopWithPooledClientsJvmTest.kt | stopWithAPooledClient | <2s | 1 | separated | good 10ms, bad 30s | good: the stop closes the pooled client's connection without waiting for its answer, about 10 ms observed per test; bad: the stop waits for a client that never answers, the whole 30 000 ms grace period (the test's withTimeout of 5 s ends it first)
kuicksilver-quic/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/quic/api/ShutdownTest.kt | aNewClientIsRefusedPromptly | <10s | 1 | separated | good 0.1s, bad 30s | good: the late client refused at its first Initial; bad: a client never refused, which gives up at its 30 s handshake timeout
kuicksilver-quic/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/quic/api/ShutdownTest.kt | anIdleEndpointShutsDownAtOnce | <5s | 1 | separated | good 10ms, bad 20s | good: an endpoint with no connections returns from shutdown at once, about 1 ms observed; bad: it waits out the 20 s grace period (the test's withTimeout of 10 s ends it first)
kuicksilver-quic/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/quic/api/ShutdownTest.kt | anInFlightTransferCompletesDuringTheGracePeriod | <10s | 1 | separated | good 0.1s, bad 20s | good: the 512 KiB transfer finishes and shutdown returns once the client closes, about 0.1 s observed; bad: shutdown waits out its 20 s grace period after the last connection closed
kuicksilver-quic/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/quic/api/ShutdownTest.kt | theDeadlineClosesWhatIsLeft | <5s | 1 | justified | good 0.3s, bad 30s | upper side of a two-sided window: good is shutdown's 300 ms grace period then the close, about 0.31 s observed; bad is a deadline that never closes the open connection, ended by the test's 30 s withTimeout; 4.7 s of headroom a loaded machine cannot use up
kuicksilver-quic/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/quic/api/ShutdownTest.kt | theDeadlineClosesWhatIsLeft | >=300ms | 1 | justified | good 0.3s, bad 0s | lower side of a two-sided window: good is the 300 ms grace period, bad is a shutdown that closes at once, near 0 s; shutdown(300.milliseconds) is called after the mark, so its deadline cannot pass before 300 ms of monotonic time on any machine
kuicksilver-tls/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/tls/KslUdpSocketCloseTest.kt | closeWaitsForACallerInsideWithoutSpinning | >=300ms | 1 | justified | good 0.3s, bad 0s | lower bound of a close that waits: the clock starts before the caller inside begins its 300 ms stay, so a correct close cannot measure less on any machine; bad is a close that does not wait, near 0 s
kuicksilver-tls/src/commonTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/tls/Tls12ResumptionWindowTest.kt | negative_tls12SessionNotResumedPastTheFirstTicketsLifetime | <=5s | 1 | separated | good 2.5s, bad 8s | good: the first refused attempt after the first ticket's 2 s lifetime, plus up to 250 ms between attempts and one handshake; bad: a renewed chain that keeps resuming until the loop's 8 s cap
kuicksilver-tls/src/jvmTest/kotlin/io/kuicksilver/tls/KslUdpSocketTest.kt | closeUnblocksReceive | <10s | 1 | separated | good 0.1s, bad 30s | good: the close wakes the receive or comes before it, at once; bad: a receive that waits out its 30 s timeout
